                <pb facs="0588" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/724: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-19T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>128. Your 179, September 12, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>You will renew your informal representations concerning Durango and other
                    Agrarian laws, and state that, in view of importance of American interests
                    affected by these laws, this Government hopes that early responses will be made
                    to your informal representations.</p>
                <pb facs="0589" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/>
                <p>You will informally and discreetly continue to press for replies to your
                    representations concerning these Agrarian measures and report results.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
